# Three-AND-gate fan-out demo.
#
# Topology: input A drives two separate AND gates (a fan-out), whose
# outputs feed a third AND. Picked specifically to exercise multiple
# supplement phases at once:
#
#   - Phase 13 (Steiner trunks): wire A fans out to two consumers at
#     different x positions, so its route is one horizontal trunk
#     split at the first consumer's x, plus a vertical drop per
#     consumer. A black junction dot appears at the interior T-join.
#   - Phase 11 (IEC glyphs): the three AND gates show '&' centered.
#   - Phase 5 (junction dots): visible at the fan-out branch point.
#   - Phase 8 / 9 (black-box view): switch with Ctrl+B — three inputs
#     A, B, C on the left, one output Y on the right.
#   - Phase 7 / 10 (persistence): the layout + future @wires + @display_*
#     annotations round-trip cleanly.
#
# Logical function: Y = (A AND B) AND (A AND C)
#                     = A AND B AND C  (since A AND A == A)
# So this is a degenerate 3-input AND — but the topology is what matters.

inputs: A, B, C
outputs: Y

g1 = and(A, B)
g2 = and(A, C)
Y  = and(g1, g2)

# @layout
# @  g1 = 300, 280
# @  g2 = 450, 400
# @  Y  = 620, 340
# @  __input:A   = 100, 220
# @  __input:B   = 100, 340
# @  __input:C   = 100, 460
# @  __output:Y  = 800, 340
